meanings
  source-authoring-grammar
    defined-by relation
    definition "Finite source-description forms bind an entire authoring operation and its destination to a generated declaration in the same language grammar."
    precondition "Every byte of the request is consumed by one registered full form; path, identifier, technical type and numeric value match the declaration exactly; identifier and numeric domains are valid; explicit quoted literal ownership is handled before this contract."
    effect "Produces conditional source spans and a declaration correspondence. Additional read-first, no-write, registration, deployment or future-work clauses do not match a source-only form and retain their independent authority. No import initialization, caller effects or compilation result is certified."
    source "js/agentic/code_task.mjs sha256=8eb10eeeddfc1eafafacf191e7c13bc80f9f13040cb0005bdb2f347b56b04ee0"
    source "rust/src/agentic_coding/code_task.rs sha256=6c6305e14bf7635dba513de340770ca712e6bb0413c72d1b7314eefbd032f219"
    unit "request offsets are UTF16 in JavaScript and UTF8 in Rust"
    example "A renamed public zero-argument i64 function or a named f64 division function can match a whole source-authoring form."
    source "js/agentic/code_task/source_contract/matcher.mjs sha256=2ff1bef0ffc630981fac5a06e9690bb57d72414e0812e4778eed963848b586c5"
    source "rust/src/agentic_coding/code_task/source_contract/matcher.rs sha256=28fcc8ce3a8d69c63565bec8c553d6023ab8ccb2baea796a8edc850b0e87328b"
    source "data/seed/source-authoring-grammar.lino sha256=f1f1ebc9f375cd838f1f5087f4f4de08de8c350f3ba0759c5b4e875de7df3d42"
